{"type":"record","name":"IbkrPreOpenStrikeStatus","namespace":"app.options.ibkr.gex","doc":"Per-strike pre-open status on the STRIKE PLANE (rev13 section 0), keyed symbol|expiry|strike. Published to options.ibkr.gex.status by databento-gex-service's pre-open IBKR GEX publisher (IbkrPreOpenService). That topic carried hand-built JSON strings until the 2026-10-18 cutover, which ROLLED IT FORWARD under its own name - the topic was wiped and recreated carrying Avro, not renamed to a versioned sibling: topics in this estate are rolled forward under their own name and versioned topic names are being removed. This record reproduces that JSON FIELD FOR FIELD AND NAME FOR NAME. That is a hard requirement, not tidiness: the feed gateway converts these records to JSON for the browser with AvroJson, which emits exactly the published record's own fields, and option-chain.js reads them BY NAME. Renaming or retyping a field here changes what the browser receives. The registry subject is this record's FULL NAME, under RecordNameStrategy. That is deliberate and not the Confluent default, and here it is load-bearing rather than merely conventional: this ONE topic carries nine distinct value shapes, and a topic-name subject could not hold nine schemas. It also keeps one subject across environments, where TopicNameStrategy would mint a different subject per environment because the topic name carries the environment's TOPIC_PREFIX.","fields":[{"name":"state","type":"string","doc":"Strike-plane state: FRESH, STALE, GATED or ABSENT. A STRING, not an Avro enum. The strike plane, the path plane and the generation control each draw from a different vocabulary, so one shared enum would have to be the union of all three and would assert less, not more; and a new state would be unreadable to every consumer compiled against the old schema rather than merely unrecognised. The vocabulary is instead closed on the PRODUCER side: each record is built only through its sealed carrier, whose constructor takes the corresponding Java enum, so an unlisted state is unrepresentable at the publication boundary."},{"name":"reasonCodes","type":{"type":"array","items":"string"},"doc":"Why the state is what it is, in producer order. Empty array when the state needs no qualification; never null, because the JSON always emitted at least []."},{"name":"sessionId","type":"string","doc":"Publishing session identity, so a consumer can tell one service lifetime's records from another's."},{"name":"outputGeneration","type":"long","doc":"The output generation in force when this status was published. Monotonic per trade date and never reused; the recovery reader mints strictly above the maximum it observes."},{"name":"baselineEpoch","type":"long","doc":"The open-interest baseline epoch this status was judged against, or 0 when none was active. A DISTINCT counter from outputGeneration: the two are independent and must never alias."},{"name":"recordRevision","type":"long","doc":"Monotonic revision of this strike's record, used by the consumer to discard a stale replay of the same key."},{"name":"eventTimeMs","type":"long","doc":"Event time in epoch milliseconds. The browser anchors its server clock from the first present of serverTimeMs, eventTimeMs, atMs, effectiveTimeMs, so this field's NAME is part of the contract."}]}